# Oblivion Ring's leaves ability returns "the exiled card to the battlefield under its owner's control" - not its own
# controller's. Bot1's Oblivion Ring exiles Bot1's own Llanowar Elves (it may: "another target nonland permanent"). With
# Opalescence on the battlefield the Ring is a 3/3 creature (CR 613.1d), so Bot2 takes it with Act of Treason (CR 613.1b)
# and bolts it: it leaves under Bot2's control, so the leaves ability is Bot2's (CR 603.3a), and it returns the Elves under
# the control of its owner, Bot1 (CR 110.2a). The Ring goes to its owner's graveyard, Bot1's (CR 400.3).

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Opalescence
Oblivion Ring
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
